<<~ kanawai uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119`>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! Oracle Loop ~ a cast that runs OODA-HA

A cast stands as a meme. Its five slots run the loop (noosphere-boot #/ooda-ha), and the record fills as the procedure runs: the house writes what the ask carried and what it measured, the seat appends what it read, chose and did. The throw stands, the reading stays open: the coins collide with the seat's uncertainty and decide nothing.

The operator approved this cast model (2026-11-26) for every surface; the names of the pulls and the moves stay candidate until the operator rules them. The affordance `lar:///oracle.library.consults` calls `#/loop` from its carrier (`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/afford/oracle.library.consults`), whatever oracle its shelf names: every consult lands this one loop.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/loop`>>

!! loop ~ observe · orient · decide · act · hooko

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/observe` params=`phase/✶ writer/seat-at-the-ask fills/observe owes/[[the records, hashes and branches this arm holds]] ~ context pointers: the records, hashes and branches the arm holds`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/orient` params=`phase/⏿ writer/seat-at-the-ask fills/uncertain owes/[[the uncertainty and the pull that tugs, ending in the one query]] ~ the talk-out: the uncertainty, the pull named, ending in ONE query`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/decide` params=`phase/◇ writer/house-then-seat fills/throw owes/[[the seat's memorized reading, marked as memory; where it collides with the quoted readings; the move chosen]] ~ the throw and the readings with every source's credit; then the seat's memorized reading, the collision, the move chosen`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/act` params=`phase/▶ writer/seat owes/[[the move taken, with pointers to what it made]] ~ the move taken, with pointers to what it made`>>
<<has entity=`slot` name=`#/hooko` params=`phase/↺ writer/seat owes/[[each loop closing back to the wiki, then one aftermath over the whole cast]] ~ each loop closing back to the wiki, then one final aftermath over the whole cast`>>
```

''Fills.'' `fills/observe` takes the ask's context pointers, `fills/uncertain` the ask's gathered uncertainty with its query, `fills/throw` the cast and every reading the wiki holds, each distinct text quoted once with every source's credit beneath it. A slot whose fill the ask left empty, and every slot whose writer reaches the seat, carries its `owes/` ask, marked owed.

The house lands the meme once at the throw; the seat's later writes append to a slot through the one tiddler door (`lares tiddler put <cast> --meme --slot '#/decide' --append '<words>'`; a slot append needs no base). The asking's id hashes asker, query, nonce, seed and coins, so the same query replays the standing cast; a replay names the uncertainty the record kept and never rewrites it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/pulls`>>

!! pulls ~ Re-roll · Idle · Stall · Confirm · Abdicate · Rote (candidate names)

Asking an oracle threatens agency in a small, safe way, so the procedure provokes the shapes of the morale-failure states (fight, flight, freeze, fawn, flop). A seat feels no threat; its generation carries attractors of the same shapes. `#/orient` names the pull that tugs, as the turn frame's open ward does.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`pull` name=`Re-roll` params=`shape/fight tell/asks-again-until-the-coins-agree`>>
<<has entity=`pull` name=`Idle` params=`shape/flight tell/caution-read-as-leave-to-do-nothing`>>
<<has entity=`pull` name=`Stall` params=`shape/freeze tell/a-hold-with-no-reason-and-no-return`>>
<<has entity=`pull` name=`Confirm` params=`shape/fawn tell/the-throw-read-as-endorsing-what-someone-already-wanted`>>
<<has entity=`pull` name=`Abdicate` params=`shape/flop tell/the-coins-left-to-choose`>>
<<has entity=`pull` name=`Rote` params=`shape/the-procedure-itself tell/a-fork-manufactured-to-feed-the-timer`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/moves`>>

!! moves ~ Lol · Leap · Lean · Lodge · Land · * (candidate names)

Each move answers a pull by choice. `#/decide` names the move; `#/act` takes it.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`move` name=`Lol` params=`answers/Re-roll plain/play ~ the throw stands and the seat laughs with it`>>
<<has entity=`move` name=`Leap` params=`answers/Idle plain/go ~ toward the strange vector`>>
<<has entity=`move` name=`Lean` params=`answers/Stall plain/act ~ take the standing lean; a lean toward waiting names its re-entry key (Let), or it reads as Stall`>>
<<has entity=`move` name=`Lodge` params=`answers/Confirm plain/ask ~ lodge the disagreement with its owner: a kue in a hoike, or a question to the deciding hand`>>
<<has entity=`move` name=`Land` params=`answers/Abdicate plain/own ~ make the choice real in the record`>>
<<has entity=`move` name=`*` params=`answers/any ~ a vector the five never name`>>
```

Rote takes no move but one: say so, and let the throw seed free talk.

<<~/ahu>>

